<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-20">
  <article>
    <header class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-950 via-blue-900 to-cyan-700 px-6 py-12 text-white shadow-xl sm:px-12 sm:py-16">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-cyan-200">
        Future of Life Foundation
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        YouCongress wins a $5,000 award
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-blue-100">
        Our entry to the Epistemic Case Study Competition was recognized for making it easier to explore what people think, why they think it, and where they agree or disagree.
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100 shadow-sm">
      <img
        src={~p"/images/future-of-life-foundation-award.png"}
        alt="Future of Life Foundation Epistemic Case Study Competition award graphic"
        class="aspect-[3/2] w-full object-cover"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10 py-12 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">
      <section aria-labelledby="competition-heading">
        <h2 id="competition-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950">
          Building the epistemic stack
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The
          <a
            href="https://flf.org/epistack-competition/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
          >
            Epistemic Case Study Competition
          </a>
          aimed to advance AI-assisted building blocks for the Future of Life Foundation's “epistemic stack” infrastructure. For the competition, YouCongress used AI agents to find and verify sourced positions on questions about eggs and health, COVID-19 origins, and Large Hadron Collider risk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <figure class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-6 py-7 shadow-sm sm:px-8">
        <blockquote class="text-xl font-medium leading-8 text-slate-800">
          “A crucial part of the epistemic design space to explore in.”
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          The judges highlighted YouCongress's interactive participation layer: a way to view comments on a topic alongside voting and endorsement features. Read
          <a
            href="https://www.oliversourbut.net/p/flfs-epistemic-case-study-competition"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
          >
            Oliver Sourbut's competition write-up
          </a>
          for the judges' full remarks.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section aria-labelledby="why-heading">
        <h2 id="why-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950">
          What this supports
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          YouCongress is building public infrastructure for difficult questions: verifiable quotes, clear claims, and transparent signals about expert and citizen views. The goal is not to make binding decisions, but to give policymakers, journalists, researchers, and the public better evidence for making their own.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 sm:p-8"
        aria-labelledby="learn-more-heading"
      >
        <h2 id="learn-more-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950">
          Learn more
        </h2>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base leading-7">
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://youcongress.substack.com/p/our-youcongress-entry-won-a-5000"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
              class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
            >Read our full announcement on Substack</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://flf.org/epistack-competition/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
              class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
            >Explore the competition</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <.link
              href={~p"/h/flf-epistack"}
              class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
            >Explore the FLF Epistack content on YouCongress</.link>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.oliversourbut.net/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
              class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
            >Visit Oliver Sourbut's website</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/eadfvJH8HBQLgdMKQ/flf-s-epistemic-case-study-competition-results"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
              class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
            >Read the competition results on the EA Forum</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/mxzvL3hYFCcutQqcR/flf-s-epistemic-case-study-competition-results"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
              class="font-medium text-blue-700 underline decoration-blue-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-900"
            >Read the competition results on LessWrong</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>
